Finally! After around 20 years of playing rogue, hack and nethack I managed 
to ascend.  After reaching the Astral plane (with a Valkyrie) and dying 
ignominiously about 18 months ago I got distracted by my other half 
(Duncan) telling me that it was so much easier with a wizard.

However, after a spate of YAADs I decided to go for the brute force 
approach with a Valkyrie. Generally speaking things tend to go wrong around 
the castle when I don't have reflection, or I'm burdened or I just haven't 
got good enough armor/weapons. My other problem is negotiating with Duncan 
about who gets to play with the Psion Netbook. (Fortunately he now has an 
overpowered laptop with wireless connection to keep him entertained at 
least some of the time!)

BTW: this really is a *first* ascension post - the other three below are 
Duncan's. As there was a squeak of complaint that I had beaten the scores 
of all but one of his ascensions I'm not sure how much longer my score will 
survive in second place.

So, started out this time fairly steadily and carefully. Sokoban gave the 
more useful (in my view) bag of holding instead of the LONG run of amulets 
of reflections that I have had recently from the RNG.

However the bag of holding was the only really good early present from the 
RNG. I was busy searching for an altar so that I could get Mojo, but it 
wasn't until level 12 that I found one. (In the long run there were only 
about 3 in the main dungeon in this game). As luck would have it, when I 
did find the altar (co-aligned) it was also a bones level from an earlier 
Judy the Valkyrie - complete with Mojo, speed boots and +2 Gauntlets of 
power and, as I discovered later, the last two were both fireproofed. I 
think that this was also where the amulet of reflection came from, but I'm 
not quite certain. (I think the bones level was created as I was 
desperately wandering the dungeon trying to find some form of water-walking 
or levitation to get past Medusa without getting stuck). The Mojo etc were 
cursed, but fortunately I had found scrolls of remove curse by that point. 
Another useful early find was a cursed silver saber and a wand of 
cancellation - giving me the wherewithal for decent two-weaponing with 
silver damage.

>From then on things definitely looked up. I found Fort Ludios, although I 
had to retreat the first time after both pets died, and managed to buy 
enough protection from the priest in minetown to get to a naked armour 
class of 1. Fort Ludios also kindly provided the gray dragon scales I 
wanted to go with the amulet of reflection while two-weaponing. Still 
without levitation/water walking, but with Jumping Boots I dug below Medusa 
and climbed back up to kill her.  But again the RNG fought back - no boots 
of levitation in Perseus' statue for my freshly prepared holy water...

I briefly had a robe, in the hope of casting the odd spell, but 
unfortunately something (a lich I think) disintegrated it, so all liches 
then joined the earler h's I had confined to oblivion. (A recurring theme 
of my YAAD's tends to be problems with mind flayers and curses/lost armour 
thanks to liches). When I found another scroll of genocide R's bought it 
too (more damaged/destroyed armour!).

Despite the odd accident with pets - like pushing my pet mummy into a pit 
and killing it while blind (sorry Odin!) I made it down to the castle in 
one piece and fairly well equipped. Short game of mastermind and with the 
help of my then pet (a Yellow Dragon) cleared out the castle without too 
many problems.  I didn't get a wish from the throne in the castle, but the 
wand of wishing gave me a useful selection of weapon/armour upgrades thanks 
to a magic marker, plus a blessed ring of levitation (having found just 
about every *other* type of ring!) and 7 blessed wax candles (minetown only 
had 4).

So, on to Gehennom. This was mostly fairly straightforward, although I went 
through a series of pets that unfortunately weren't chunky enough. A couple 
of slightly nasty moments with Jubilex (who made me
sick) and Asmodeus but I made it through and the only annoying thing with 
Orcus was that his wand of death disintegrated when I killed him with Mojo. 
The *really* annoying thing was searching for Vlad's tower
- I never had much in the way of light sources and by the time I realized I 
had missed the stairs I didn't have any light source. Fortunately the 
systematic approach eventually got there. (Including reading the Gazeteer 
*properly* to realize that the entrance is within a specific range of 
levels below the Valley of the Dead).

Finally to the Wizard's tower (found the vibrating square earlier while 
searching for Vlad's tower). I used one of my remaining wishes for a 
blessed figurine of an Archon, which was a fairly good move. The only 
annoying thing was that Archy wasn't very good at coming when called... 
Killed Rodney the first time with Mojo and then moved down to the amulet - 
again not too difficult with Archy's help. (Reflection with fooproof 
everything and all of the resistances also helps).

As always climbing back up with the Amulet was a bit annoying as I kept 
slipping back down, but Rodney mostly died fairly quickly with my wands of 
death and I was actually quite lucky with how rarely I needed to uncurse 
things - I don't think that anything important ever got worse than 
uncursed. Rather surprisingly I was left with a large pile of holy water 
and scrolls of remove curse at the end.

Finally back to level 1. Acting on advice received I dropped the amulet and 
nipped back to my cache to drop the unnecessary things and pick up as many 
wands of fire, lightning, digging and teleporation as possible. (And, no, I 
don't know why two of the wands of teleportation were fireproofed!).

Next to the Plane of Earth. On cue Rodney appeared, but left again almost 
immediately thanks to my wand of death. Confusion + scroll of gold 
detection showed the portal nearby and I got there without any serious 
problems. The Plane of Air wasn't a serious problem, nor the Plane of Fire 
- apart from the time spent waiting for Archy to finish playing!. The 
biggest problem I had was in deciding whether or not to save my final 
scroll of gold detection for the Plane of Water, before remembering that I 
was carrying the Orb of Fate (doh!).

At last - the Astral Plane, after a slight worry because Archy went through 
the portal without me. I arrived in the SW corner and, after working out 
that Death was at the West end of the plane, started heading to the East-
most altar (yes I'm a coward at heart). Acquired a tame Angel who was quite 
useful and struggled a little bit with the tide of monsters until I 
remembered to use the wands of teleportation I had brought. Surprisingly 
easily I got to the east-most altar and it was the right one! (So no need 
for the helm of opposite alignment I had brought in case of desperation). 
Obviously at some point I had zapped a priest that I shouldn't have done, 
as Odin was angry with me, but fortunately not enough to stop me ascending.

